I tried to include as many non spoilery
things as possible. I also saw a lot of 

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.050
Brienne jokes.

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:17.529
So just as we get into it, careful for
spoilers from the episode if you haven't seen

00:00:17.529 --> 00:00:18.189
it yet.

00:00:18.189 --> 00:00:21.550
I think my favorite joke was when Sansa
got mad at Brienne and for being at

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:22.249
Joffery's wedding.

00:00:22.249 --> 00:00:25.359
In her defence, it's not her fault. She
wasn't there in the books.

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:28.380
So here we go, first question. Kaiser Red asks,

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.589
"Why doesn't Brienne mention the fact
that Aria lives to Sansa?

00:00:31.589 --> 00:00:35.490
Because everyone else thinks
she's dead." I think that she probably

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:38.910
just forgot and the writers probably
excluded that because they felt it

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.400
would create more problems in the
narrative of the episode.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.730
This is one of those logic issues.
Normally you would expect that Brienne

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:48.240
would say, "Hey your sister's still alive!"
And maybe that would entice Sansa to go with her and

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.850
then they go to track down Arya.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.010
But that would pull the story in a
vastly different direction than the

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:53.970
writers wanna go.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:58.070
So the convenient thing to do is just
exclude it. Just make Brienne forget to

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:58.760
mention it.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.570
As much as it seems weird you have to
remember that Briane is a normal person

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:05.710
and think about all the times you talk
to your friends and you just you forget

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:06.689
to mention things.

00:01:06.689 --> 00:01:09.700
So if you really want to nitpick you
could chalk it up to that, but really I

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:13.009
think the writers just excluded it because
they didn't want to pull the story in a

00:01:13.009 --> 00:01:14.280
different direction.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.170
Next question: Nick asks, "Could you do a
video explaining the Martell family like

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:22.429
why they're called princes?" I assume you mean
when the rest of the people in Westeros are

00:01:22.429 --> 00:01:24.409
called lords and like there's only one
king,

00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:28.340
so why are the Martells called princes? The
Martells are part of the Seven Kingdoms so

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.670
technically (like in a hierarchy)
they are lords but

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:35.119
its are Rhoynar tradition to call
yourself a prince so they give

00:01:35.119 --> 00:01:37.219
themselves the prince / princess titles

00:01:37.219 --> 00:01:40.240
for cultural reasons. It doesn't give
them extra power,

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:44.179
it's just that they're upholding traditions
of their ancestors. I may have explained in a

00:01:44.179 --> 00:01:45.659
previous video, but

00:01:45.659 --> 00:01:49.149
Princess Nymeria was a Rhoynar princess
when the Valyrians invaded

00:01:49.149 --> 00:01:50.439
their homeland in the east.

00:01:50.439 --> 00:01:54.549
She led them across the land bridge and
created what is now modern day Dorne.

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:57.889
So when people talk about Rhoynar traditions
they're talking about those people.

00:01:57.889 --> 00:02:01.509
Next question: Chris asks,"What do you
think the significance of Drogon

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:03.029
sniffing Danny's hand

00:02:03.029 --> 00:02:07.249
and flying away is?" Well I think that they
included that just to show that the

00:02:07.249 --> 00:02:09.650
Dragons haven't lost their bond with the
Daenerys.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:12.660
Drogon is still bonded to her even
though he's flying free.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.950
It's a contrast to Rhaegal and Viserion
who

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:18.950
are chained up beneath the pyramid and
going crazy. Dan and Dave just don't want

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:22.310
you to be confused and think that the
dragons have completely turned on her.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:25.180
They haven't, like the dragons that are
chained up are just really pissed.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.459
Daenerys also made it seem like Drogon
had left for good, so

00:02:28.459 --> 00:02:32.040
it's just a reminder the Drogon is
not gone for good. It's like he's just

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.430
checking in with Mom before he goes
off and has some more fun.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:38.769
Next question: Kevin asks, "I think John Snow will
