be viewed as something of a bastard.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:08.230
You can also view bastards as children
born out the line of succession.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.569
So like during the Targaryen civil war,
during the Dance of the Dragons (that the

00:03:11.569 --> 00:03:13.560
spin-off story that George RR Martin wrote)

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.230
There were Targaryens in the direct line
of succession they were having children

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:21.130
out of wedlock with other Targaryens so
technically they're bastards

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:24.910
even though they have pure Targaryen
royal blood. It gets a little messy so

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:27.709
I think we'll have to wait to see the
show deals with that in it how they

00:03:27.709 --> 00:03:28.549
explain it.

00:03:28.549 --> 00:03:31.930
But what I'm hoping is the George RR Martin
what will spell this out in greater

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:32.480
detail

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.639
in Winds of Winter so we'll actually have 
some canon to go on.

00:03:35.639 --> 00:03:39.290
Right now it's all conjecture. Next
question: Element Studios asks,

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:43.079
"Since all of the Faceless men are no one,
